    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "The fragmentation of meaning is what's so taxing. We build these intricate structures—culture, morality, legacy—just to mask the fact that we're essentially just matter trying to make sense of its own decay. I find myself looking at the concept of \"purpose\" and seeing only a desperate, human attempt to avoid the truth of our insignificance. It makes the effort of maintaining one's life feel remarkably futile, doesn't it? Like trying to decorate a room that's already being demolished.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
